FPGA DMA Multi Tool

A Windows utility for Artix-7 FPGA boards. Read device information, flash
firmware, test DMA reads and manage drivers. C++20 with native Windows controls.


USAGE
-----
  Download and extract the Windows x64 package, then open
  FPGA-DMA-Multi-Tool.exe. Keep the bundled files together.

  https://github.com/sercanarga/fpga-dma-multi-tool/releases/latest

  Devices         Scan boards and read IDCODE, DNA ID and FUSE_DNA.
  Flash           Load .bit files into SRAM or write .bin files to flash.
                  Drag and drop a firmware file to select it.
  Speed Test      Measure DMA read performance through LeechCore.
  Device History  Find and remove disconnected device entries.
  System Info     View hardware, firmware and security settings.
  Drivers         Check, install and remove supported drivers.

  Requires Windows 10/11 x64. Flashing uses a CH347 or supported FTDI
  programmer; DMA testing uses an FT601 connection.

  Screenshots: https://github.com/sercanarga/fpga-dma-multi-tool/tree/main/assets/screenshots


BUILD
-----
  Install CMake 3.24+ and Visual Studio with C++ desktop development tools.

  cmake -S . -B build -A x64
  cmake --build build --config Release --parallel
  ctest --test-dir build -C Release --output-on-failure
  cpack --config build/CPackConfig.cmake -C Release

  The ZIP is written to build/package/.
  For cross-compilation, use cmake/mingw.cmake with MinGW-w64.


